<title>BRAZIL: Trade in Banespa to resume Monday.</title>
<headline>Trade in Banespa to resume Monday.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading in Sao Paulo's Banespa bank will resume Monday at 1100 local/1400 GMT on the local stock exchanges after a seven-day suspension, said Brazil's Securities and Exchange Commission (CVM).</p>
<p>The CVM said trading will resume after Banespa's latest statement explaining details of a debt rescheduling accord.</p>
<p>Last week Sao Paulo state and the federal government finalized a major debt restructuring deal under which a controlling stake in Banespa was transferred to federal hands.</p>
<p>((--Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 2485412))</p>
